  "observations": {
    "core": "Inspected first and second endings12/13 and new repeated section14. Candidate imposes spurious melody chords over the descending triplets in both endings. At12:3 a separate Bb3 quarter overlaps the triplet accompaniment, rather than replacing its first note. At13 last two third-beat subdivisions have shared upper/lower stems on chords. At14 there are shared stems and distinct melody versus triplet durations.",
    "marks": "12 first-ending bracket, dim. near1, mf near3, upper Eb4@4/3 fingering3,Bb3@7/3=2,Bb3 melody@3=3; lower Ab3@4/3=1,D3 final=1. 13 second-ending bracket: upper Eb4@4/3=3,Bb3@7/3=2,final first chord lower member=1 and upper=3; lower G3@4/3=1,Eb3@3=1,Bb2@10/3=2.14 p,accent on Cb5,digit5 onAb4 short note,Ab4@2 substitution4->5 with lowerF4=2; final chord fingering upper3/lower1 at3. Staccato dots on final two short chord groups and short slur.",
    "route": "First ending12 closes with backward repeat to2. Second ending13 follows and closes before forward repeat14. Preserve both ending brackets and physical bars; no duplication of bars in XML. Playback should visit1,2..12,2..11,13,14... .",
    "accidentals": "Upper12/13 Anatural3 in descending line; upper12 explicit flat on Bb3 melody at3. Upper13 final chords Eb4+Gb4 then F4+Ab4 with explicit Gb/Ab glyphs.14 Gb4 and Cb5/Cb4 explicit flats, F4 natural at2 (not an altered sounding pitch inferred from the natural glyph). Lower14 Gb octave flats.",
    "accidental_carry_recheck": "Explicit Gb4 at0 continues within its physical bar: later G4-position notes in14\u201317 and20/21 sound Gb4 unless a natural cancels it. Missing repeated glyph is not natural. Updated working targets before any freeze.",
    "bar13_lower_resolution": "Close lower crop confirms m013-s2-v1-e13 D3 eighth-triplet at3 (middle bass line), thenBb2@10/3,Ab2@11/3 with explicit flat. Earlier marks text saying Eb3@3 was wrong; fingering1 belongs toD3@3. Retain D3 pitch. Shared upper chords at10/3 and11/3 have upper and lower beam/stem membership, and must have one sounding onset per member, not two MIDI attacks.",
    "bar11_ending_tie_resolution": "The low curved continuation under bass Bb2whole11 ends atBb2quarter12:0 on first traversal, and atBb2quarter13:0 on second traversal. Encode tie start on11 bassBb2 with alternate-route stop members12/13, never a tie12->13. Exact existing source IDs: m011-s2-v2-e02 (pitch itself corrected toBb2), m012-s2-v2-e02 and m013-s2-v2-e02 are confirmed original stop members. Same source split applies to moving-line phrase slur across endings; exact distal endpoint still open."
  },
